WEBVTT

00:00:25.718 --> 00:00:29.698
RECORD OF LODOSS WAR
Chronicles of the Heroic Knight

00:00:29.722 --> 00:00:33.556
RECORD OF LODOSS WAR
Chronicles of the Heroic Knight

00:01:46.299 --> 00:01:49.200
It has been two days since
Orson and the others were...

00:01:49.268 --> 00:01:52.203
...defeated by Ashram in the
battle at the pirates' hideout.

00:01:52.271 --> 00:01:56.230
Now captives, they are on their
way to Blue Dragon Island aboard...

00:01:56.309 --> 00:01:59.609
...the Marmo military
ship "Sea Devil's Horn".

00:01:59.679 --> 00:02:03.081
I see. I figured they
were sent from Flaim.

00:02:03.382 --> 00:02:06.818
And with a berserker among them...
You're sure of this?

00:02:06.886 --> 00:02:11.517
| can faintly sense the workings of
the spirit which controls his mind.

00:02:12.658 --> 00:02:15.218
And the spirit of
anger within him...

00:02:15.294 --> 00:02:18.696
...can blaze to life
like burning hot lava.

00:02:18.831 --> 00:02:19.798
Fascinating.

00:02:19.865 --> 00:02:24.894
There's no way he can consciously
control his berserker strength?

00:02:24.971 --> 00:02:26.871
Impossible.

00:02:26.939 --> 00:02:28.429
I see.

00:02:28.507 --> 00:02:31.204
Except, that time...

00:02:31.277 --> 00:02:35.544
When I felt the spirit of anger
releasing me from its spell...

00:02:35.614 --> 00:02:40.313
...called it back because I still
needed its power to fight with.

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:45.223
Can it be |I don't really
WANT to escape the spirit's spell?

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.991
Or- Orson...

00:03:00.072 --> 00:03:01.233
Orson!

00:03:01.307 --> 00:03:02.866
Whoops! Sorry about that!

00:03:02.942 --> 00:03:04.876
<i>Y-You...!</i>

00:03:05.378 --> 00:03:06.402
Damn it!

00:03:06.479 --> 00:03:09.176
Shirts! Don't try to move!

00:03:09.248 --> 00:03:13.116
I'm all right... I just
got a little careless before!

00:03:14.153 --> 00:03:16.918
The next time we fight,
you won't beat me.

00:03:16.989 --> 00:03:19.321
Oh, really?
I'll take you on any time...

00:03:19.392 --> 00:03:21.053
.little girl.

00:03:21.127 --> 00:03:23.095
Damn it...!

00:03:26.499 --> 00:03:27.432
Shirts.

00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:30.299
| swear!
Next time, I'll beat her!

00:03:30.369 --> 00:03:34.067
Shirts... There's no way
you can beat that woman warrior.

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:38.134
You'll lose next time you fight
her and then again after that.

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:40.235
Don't be such a know-it-all!

00:03:40.312 --> 00:03:42.076
She's just a giant with
a lot of brute strength!

00:03:42.148 --> 00:03:45.641
In an honest sword fight,
she'd never beat me!

00:03:46.118 --> 00:03:49.053
In a strict test of swordsmanship,
you probably would win.

00:03:49.121 --> 00:03:51.886
But real battle is dif ferent.
And you know it.

00:03:51.957 --> 00:03:53.083
Just drop the subject!

00:03:53.159 --> 00:03:56.288
I don't think
you could even beat me.

00:03:56.495 --> 00:03:58.930
You might be able to hurt me...

00:03:58.998 --> 00:04:02.161
...but the one to score the first
lethal wound...would be me.

00:04:02.234 --> 00:04:04.134
| said DROP IT, okay?!

00:04:04.203 --> 00:04:08.436
You're way out of line on this,
Orson! Next time, I won't lose!

00:04:08.507 --> 00:04:11.841
And not for Lodoss's
sake or for Parn's sake, either!

00:04:11.911 --> 00:04:15.848
For the sake of my own pride,
I have to beat that woman!

00:04:17.049 --> 00:04:19.609
I'm sorry, Shirts.

00:04:19.819 --> 00:04:22.789
| wasn't strong enough, either...

00:04:25.524 --> 00:04:29.688
Orson, you're crying. Does this mean
you're getting your feelings back?

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:37.861
Ashram and his party have reached
Blue Dragon Island.

00:04:37.937 --> 00:04:39.871
Home of Abram the sea dragon.

00:04:39.939 --> 00:04:42.874
There he seeks to gain
the Governor's Treasure...

00:04:42.942 --> 00:04:45.138
...known as
"The Scepter of Domination".

00:04:45.311 --> 00:04:48.747
Ashram has brought Orson with him,
with his purpose being...

00:04:48.814 --> 00:04:53.115
...to have a living witness to the
successful completion of his goal.

00:04:56.388 --> 00:04:59.483
I hope Abram has the
scepter in his possession.

00:04:59.558 --> 00:05:03.791
If he does, then Sir Ashram's journey
will end here at Blue Dragon Island.

00:05:04.063 --> 00:05:07.465
No. Once I possess
the Scepter of Domination,

00:05:07.533 --> 00:05:09.592
the true battle will begin.

00:05:09.668 --> 00:05:13.002
The battle to unite
all of Lodoss awaits.

00:05:14.306 --> 00:05:16.400
There it is...

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.009
That's Abram, the sea dragon?!

00:05:23.382 --> 00:05:24.406
Let's go!

00:05:24.483 --> 00:05:26.178
A moment, please!

00:05:26.252 --> 00:05:29.244
Let me start by trying
to negotiate with him.

00:05:29.321 --> 00:05:30.254
Negotiate?

00:05:30.322 --> 00:05:31.983
Yes.

00:05:33.893 --> 00:05:35.054
Go to it.

00:05:35.127 --> 00:05:37.186
Well, then...
| dare say that,

00:05:38.564 --> 00:05:42.501
if we get the Scepter of
Domination without a fight...

00:05:42.568 --> 00:05:45.765
...then nothing will stand in our way.

00:05:54.446 --> 00:05:58.280
Who is it that disturbs my slumber?

00:05:59.318 --> 00:06:03.755
A human. I could tell you my name,
but it would mean nothing to you.

00:06:04.223 --> 00:06:06.658
I have no use for humans.

00:06:06.725 --> 00:06:10.252
They are puny creatures,
and easy prey to fire.

00:06:10.396 --> 00:06:15.391
| suggest you leave immediately.
| wish to sleep.

00:06:15.801 --> 00:06:18.827
Abram, I wish to ask you something.

00:06:18.938 --> 00:06:22.704
Is it true that the treasure you
guard is the Scepter of Domination?

00:06:22.775 --> 00:06:26.643
No, it is not. You have
no business here. Now leave!

00:06:27.379 --> 00:06:30.212
What about the Soul Crystal Ball?

00:06:30.282 --> 00:06:32.808
| do indeed possess that.

00:06:32.885 --> 00:06:38.289
Master Wagnard! The search is over!
I've found the Soul Crystal Ball!

00:06:39.024 --> 00:06:43.393
If you are saying you're here
to steal the Governor's Treasure...

00:06:43.596 --> 00:06:46.531
...then I've no choice
but to stop you.

00:06:46.599 --> 00:06:49.864
You shall suffer
a most unfortunate end.

00:06:50.336 --> 00:06:54.170
No, Abram. It is you who
will suffer that unfortunate end!

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:57.266
Then to me,
you are merely thieves!

00:07:01.380 --> 00:07:02.814
How did the negotiations go?

00:07:02.881 --> 00:07:08.149
They broke down. Abram
definitely doesn't have the scepter.

00:07:08.887 --> 00:07:13.518
But, since he's angry that we disturbed
his sleep, he wants to devour us.

00:07:14.526 --> 00:07:15.755
Then we have no choice.

00:07:15.828 --> 00:07:18.160
You! Stay here and watch!

00:07:18.697 --> 00:07:20.426
Let's go!

00:07:22.534 --> 00:07:24.525
Hobb! Sing the song of battle!

00:07:24.603 --> 00:07:27.595
The sound of a dragon's roar
can shatter a man's resolve!

00:07:27.673 --> 00:07:29.038
Protect us from that!

00:07:29.108 --> 00:07:31.304
By your command!

00:07:46.592 --> 00:07:49.584
|-- I'm scared! I want to run!

00:07:49.662 --> 00:07:51.926
<i>Can this be.. fear?!</i>

00:07:58.937 --> 00:08:00.803
Let's go!

00:08:03.842 --> 00:08:06.812
"I call forth the power
of the mighty kraken!"

00:08:13.752 --> 00:08:17.689
Abram's movements were dulled
by his recent hibernation.

00:08:18.791 --> 00:08:21.988
He breathed fire,
thrashed his tail...

00:08:22.494 --> 00:08:25.555
...and fought back with
magical lightning attacks.

00:08:25.631 --> 00:08:28.692
But, in the end,
he could not withstand...

00:08:28.767 --> 00:08:32.431
...the terrific onslaught
of Ashram and his party.

00:08:32.938 --> 00:08:34.872
Finally...

00:08:58.530 --> 00:09:01.397
Wh- Wh- What are you doing to me?

00:09:01.467 --> 00:09:04.801
"Myrii. Give peace
to this man's heart.”

00:09:08.407 --> 00:09:09.932
You'll be all right now.

00:09:10.008 --> 00:09:11.305
You won?

00:09:11.377 --> 00:09:12.902
Yes, we won. Somehow.

00:09:12.978 --> 00:09:15.276
But it was a pointless battle.

00:09:25.924 --> 00:09:27.551
What is that in your hands?

00:09:27.626 --> 00:09:30.618
Yes, sir.
It is the Soul Crystal Ball.

00:09:30.696 --> 00:09:34.929
Soul Crystal Ball? Isn't that also
one of the Governor's Treasures?

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:37.901
It's used to summon the
souls of the dead, is it not?

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:42.271
We still haven't studied it,
so I cannot give a definite answer.

00:09:42.841 --> 00:09:45.902
You look quite happy.
Shouldn't you be upset...

00:09:45.978 --> 00:09:49.710
...that I now have to
battle Shooting Star as well?

00:09:50.149 --> 00:09:53.779
Please forgive me. This may be my
poor manners as a sorcerer showing...

00:09:53.852 --> 00:09:57.015
...but I wish to begin an immediate
study of the Soul Crystal Ball.

00:09:58.223 --> 00:10:00.317
We must return to Flaim
immediately and then

00:10:00.392 --> 00:10:01.951
set off for Fire Dragon Mountain!

00:10:02.027 --> 00:10:05.019
We can't let Kashue beat us there!

00:10:08.934 --> 00:10:12.598
Master Wagnard! Master Wagnard!
Rejoice, my lord!

00:10:13.572 --> 00:10:18.442
Master Wagnard.
I have gotten the Soul Crystal Ball!

00:10:19.244 --> 00:10:21.770
You've done it, Groder!
Now all that remains...

00:10:21.847 --> 00:10:24.748
...is for you to return the
Soul Crystal Ball here safely!

00:10:24.817 --> 00:10:25.613
Yes, sir.

00:10:25.684 --> 00:10:28.517
What you must do now
is avoid all risks!

00:10:28.587 --> 00:10:31.784
Above all, do not
fight Shooting Star!

00:10:31.857 --> 00:10:34.417
He is the strongest
and mightiest dragon there is!

00:10:34.493 --> 00:10:38.361
| doubt even Ashram
can defeat that fire dragon!

00:10:38.797 --> 00:10:42.927
In any case, you've done well!
Come back here at once!

00:10:43.502 --> 00:10:45.800
Come back at once?

00:10:48.240 --> 00:10:51.642
He doesn't regret
just using me like a tool.

00:10:51.844 --> 00:10:54.939
Is he planning
to dispose of me now?

00:10:55.714 --> 00:10:59.810
Master Groder. Sir Ashram asks
that you come to him immediately.

00:10:59.885 --> 00:11:02.513
I see. I'll come at once.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.028
What's wrong, everyone?

00:11:10.095 --> 00:11:12.655
He's dif ferent. His expression...

00:11:12.731 --> 00:11:15.029
Then this must mean...

00:11:15.100 --> 00:11:18.968
Orson, you're cured!
You've gotten your emotions back!

00:11:19.171 --> 00:11:23.039
Y- You think so? I don't really
understand why, but...

00:11:23.275 --> 00:11:26.267
That look on his face
tells me it's definite!

00:11:26.345 --> 00:11:28.074
We've gotta show
this to everyone else!

00:11:28.146 --> 00:11:31.047
All right! Now we have
to escape, no matter what!

00:11:31.116 --> 00:11:34.518
That's something for
our leader to decide. Right?

00:11:34.586 --> 00:11:36.953
Yeah. Let's think of a plan.

00:11:37.022 --> 00:11:38.751
When we run,
we're all going together!

00:11:38.824 --> 00:11:40.155
Right, Leader!

00:11:40.225 --> 00:11:43.160
Well, I'M gonna try
to escape on my own!

00:11:45.097 --> 00:11:47.828
While Orson and the others
work on their escape plan...

00:11:47.900 --> 00:11:51.564
...8layn and Leylia visit
Raiden's defense force.

00:11:51.737 --> 00:11:55.401
They explain what's happened so far
to Capt. Genner of the defense forces...

00:11:55.474 --> 00:11:59.035
...and ask for a rescue party to be
sent out after Orson and the others.

00:11:59.111 --> 00:12:01.375
| understand how worried
you are about your friends...

00:12:01.446 --> 00:12:05.940
...but I have responsibilities of my
own. I can't spare you any troops.

00:12:06.018 --> 00:12:07.179
| see...

00:12:07.252 --> 00:12:11.382
| suppose we've no choice but to
go and rescue them ourselves.

00:12:11.456 --> 00:12:14.323
Impossible. Without
fighters to escort us...

00:12:14.393 --> 00:12:17.419
...magic users
like us can't fight!

00:12:19.131 --> 00:12:21.293
Did somebody say they needed
some fighters to escort them?

00:12:21.366 --> 00:12:24.165
In that case,
we'd be glad to help you out.

00:12:24.236 --> 00:12:25.931
Parn!

00:12:26.071 --> 00:12:29.473
You should be quieter
when discussing secrets.

00:12:29.541 --> 00:12:33.000
Your voice carries quite
a distance outside.

00:12:46.491 --> 00:12:49.517
You got it? I'll draw him in, okay?

00:12:53.632 --> 00:12:55.100
Hey! Got your food here!

00:12:55.167 --> 00:12:56.965
Shirts... Watch your step.

00:12:57.035 --> 00:12:59.800
Took you long enough!
You trying to starve us to death?!

00:12:59.871 --> 00:13:02.806
You should be happy
we're feeding you at all!

00:13:02.874 --> 00:13:06.037
"Pixies of rest, spirits of sleep.”

00:13:06.111 --> 00:13:06.976
"Send your dust into his eyes..."

00:13:07.045 --> 00:13:07.705
What the...?

00:13:07.779 --> 00:13:10.009
"And send him to
the land of dreams."

00:13:10.082 --> 00:13:14.815
"Silence, darkness, quiet death.
Meim Reim Alreem..."

00:13:15.687 --> 00:13:17.246
That's... That Low Ancient!

00:13:17.322 --> 00:13:19.689
Don't tell me he's chanting a spell!

00:13:19.758 --> 00:13:21.692
M- Maar...

00:13:25.397 --> 00:13:31.200
"Oblivion. Peace of mind.
Mime Rime Alreem.."

00:13:31.269 --> 00:13:36.230
"Silence, darkness, take on new
life. Leera Medeera Ru..."

00:13:38.043 --> 00:13:40.535
Nothing personal, guys.

00:13:49.454 --> 00:13:52.446
Uh-oh! Somebody's coming!

00:13:53.692 --> 00:13:57.925
Oh, Ganeed, god of thieves!
Please let nobody be in here!

00:14:11.743 --> 00:14:14.075
Escaped prisoner!
One of the prisoners has escaped!

00:14:14.146 --> 00:14:16.012
Too late!

00:14:18.350 --> 00:14:20.079
Did they all escape?

00:14:20.152 --> 00:14:21.950
No, sir! Just a child!

00:14:22.020 --> 00:14:24.546
Wrong. It was a grass runner.

00:14:24.623 --> 00:14:26.591
Let him go.

00:14:27.225 --> 00:14:31.253
He wouldn't have...?!

00:14:45.243 --> 00:14:46.472
Somebody's coming.

00:14:46.545 --> 00:14:48.673
It's a grass runner, isn't it?

00:14:48.747 --> 00:14:50.715
What's a grass runner?

00:14:50.782 --> 00:14:54.480
They're meadow sprites.
They're another tribe like elves...

00:14:54.553 --> 00:14:57.750
...who also come from
the realm of the plant fairies.

00:14:57.823 --> 00:15:00.849
It must be Maar!
80, he's all right!

00:15:01.793 --> 00:15:03.761
Hm? Uh-oh!

00:15:06.331 --> 00:15:07.457
Oh, well.

00:15:08.667 --> 00:15:12.069
Thank goodness
everyone's still alive.

00:15:16.975 --> 00:15:19.103
Thanks a lot.
It feels better now.

00:15:19.177 --> 00:15:19.905
Forget that!

00:15:19.978 --> 00:15:23.937
You're telling me there was no way
you ALL could have escaped?!

00:15:24.015 --> 00:15:26.882
This is no time to
be asking that question.

00:15:26.952 --> 00:15:30.513
We're in luck, since he can guide
us to the pirates' hideout.

00:15:30.589 --> 00:15:34.583
Huh? N- No way! Those guys
are tough! They'll kill me!

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:37.060
They won't beat us!

00:15:37.129 --> 00:15:40.963
Because we have the great mercenary
king, King Kashue, with us!

00:15:41.032 --> 00:15:43.865
King Kashue of Flaim?
THAT guy?

00:15:44.035 --> 00:15:46.299
Yeah, so will you guide us?

00:15:46.371 --> 00:15:47.634
All... All right.

00:15:48.673 --> 00:15:51.005
Enemy attack!

00:16:09.227 --> 00:16:12.253
"Foot of the salamander,
breath of the efreet!”

00:16:12.330 --> 00:16:14.822
"Angry heart of
the ancient titans.."

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:18.393
"Manna of all creation,
become the fires of destruction!"

00:16:18.470 --> 00:16:21.030
"Vanna flame ve igloss!"

00:16:24.810 --> 00:16:27.108
Don't run! Fight!

00:16:32.784 --> 00:16:34.718
Why, you...!
You're a Marmo soldier, aren't you?!

00:16:34.786 --> 00:16:38.154
No, I'm NOT!
I'm a ship's captain for hire!

00:16:39.257 --> 00:16:41.021
Besides, who the hell are you?!

00:16:41.092 --> 00:16:45.495
Me? My name is Kashue.
You may have heard of me.

00:16:45.764 --> 00:16:52.192
What?! The mercenary king?!
What's the king of Flaim doing here!

00:16:53.238 --> 00:16:55.605
Now talk! Where are
Ashram and the others?!

00:16:55.674 --> 00:17:00.168
They... They went to Fire Dragon
Mountain! That's what he told me.

00:17:00.278 --> 00:17:01.768
Are Orson and
the others all right?!

00:17:01.847 --> 00:17:03.406
Of... Of course they are!

00:17:03.949 --> 00:17:05.383
| wonder what that ruckus is.

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:07.919
Just calm down, Orson.

00:17:08.920 --> 00:17:10.752
Sorry we're late, Orson!

00:17:10.822 --> 00:17:12.517
Parn!

00:17:12.791 --> 00:17:14.190
Is everyone all right?

00:17:14.259 --> 00:17:15.727
Parn!

00:17:15.794 --> 00:17:17.387
Shirts! What happened to you?

00:17:17.462 --> 00:17:20.022
I'm fine! It's nothing major.

00:17:20.098 --> 00:17:21.395
What are you doing here?

00:17:21.466 --> 00:17:24.333
And just as we were
about to escape, too!

00:17:24.402 --> 00:17:28.862
Well, I figured that, but we're in a
hurry, so we came to speed things up.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:31.409
Oh. Well, then I forgive you.

00:17:31.476 --> 00:17:34.502
Parn, you saved us!
Thank you so much!

00:17:34.579 --> 00:17:35.740
Orson?!

00:17:35.814 --> 00:17:38.749
It looks like the power of Hyuri,
the spirit of anger...

00:17:38.817 --> 00:17:40.080
...has gotten a lot weaker.

00:17:40.151 --> 00:17:41.414
He got his emotions back.

00:17:42.254 --> 00:17:44.746
Maar! How could you
betray us like that?!

00:17:44.823 --> 00:17:48.316
I'm sorry! It was the only
thing I could do at the time!

00:17:48.393 --> 00:17:50.487
So, what's next for us?

00:17:50.562 --> 00:17:53.395
We go after Ashram and
head for Fire Dragon Mountain.

00:17:53.465 --> 00:17:56.765
We can't let him get
the Scepter of Domination!

00:17:56.835 --> 00:17:58.200
I'm going, too!

00:17:58.270 --> 00:17:59.260
In your condition?

00:17:59.337 --> 00:18:01.999
You should really go back to
the city and rest...

00:18:02.073 --> 00:18:03.768
| am definitely coming with you!

00:18:03.842 --> 00:18:07.005
There's someone in
their party I HAVE to beat!

00:18:07.078 --> 00:18:08.045
Shirts...

00:18:08.113 --> 00:18:10.309
I'm coming, too.

00:18:10.382 --> 00:18:12.316
I have my good name to restore!

00:18:12.384 --> 00:18:13.943
And I'm coming, too, of course!

00:18:14.019 --> 00:18:15.418
Very well.

00:18:15.487 --> 00:18:17.216
You're all welcome to come.

00:18:17.289 --> 00:18:21.920
And we can take care of both the
hated Shooting Star as well as Ashram.

00:18:28.199 --> 00:18:30.099
What... What's happened to the sky?!

00:18:30.168 --> 00:18:32.899
It's night, but it's
suddenly as bright as dawn!

00:18:32.971 --> 00:18:36.100
Raiden couldn't
be burning, could it?!

00:18:36.241 --> 00:18:38.437
I'm afraid it is.

00:18:38.510 --> 00:18:42.174
He swore to kill a hundred people
for every scale on him we scratched.

00:18:42.247 --> 00:18:45.615
Shooting Star is
attacking the city!

00:18:46.284 --> 00:18:48.343
We have to get back
to Raiden right now!

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:50.514
No. It'd do no good.

00:18:50.588 --> 00:18:53.148
But, if we don't do something,
the people of Raiden will be...!

00:18:53.224 --> 00:18:55.591
Don't say it, Parn.

00:18:55.660 --> 00:18:57.822
I'm perfectly aware
of that myself!

00:18:57.896 --> 00:19:01.355
But stopping Ashram's
ambitions comes first!

00:19:02.167 --> 00:19:06.604
It's a difficult decision, but one
that a king must sometimes make.

00:19:06.771 --> 00:19:08.500
But...

00:19:08.740 --> 00:19:11.607
This hurts King Kashue as well.

00:19:12.377 --> 00:19:16.871
But a king must consider the lives
of all, not just the life of one.

00:19:18.016 --> 00:19:22.044
We'd better hurry to Fire Dragon
Mountain as fast as we can.

00:19:22.120 --> 00:19:24.748
We still have a job to do!

00:19:25.991 --> 00:19:29.723
All right, Slayn. Let's go!
To Fire Dragon Mountain!

00:19:29.794 --> 00:19:32.764
To get the Scepter of Domination!

00:19:32.931 --> 00:19:36.458
And to end Ashram's
ambitions once and for all!

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:43.632
Welcome...

00:19:43.708 --> 00:19:45.267
...to Lodoss Island!

00:19:45.343 --> 00:19:46.777
And now, what's you've
all been waiting for...

00:19:46.845 --> 00:19:48.574
...the second part of the show!

00:19:52.650 --> 00:19:56.553
Without fighters to escort us,
magic users can't fight!

00:19:57.255 --> 00:20:00.384
Did somebody say they needed
some fighters to escort them?

00:20:00.458 --> 00:20:02.324
That voice! Parn!

00:20:02.394 --> 00:20:07.161
Sorry, but I've become a
Shamanist, so I can't escort you!

00:20:19.244 --> 00:20:22.179
All right! Now that Orson's
got his emotions back...

00:20:22.247 --> 00:20:24.807
...we've gotta get out of here...

00:20:24.883 --> 00:20:26.851
...is what I'd LIKE to say, but...

00:20:26.918 --> 00:20:29.649
Whee! We're on a boat!
We're on a boat!

00:20:29.721 --> 00:20:31.120
Is he that happy about it.

00:20:31.189 --> 00:20:33.988
Great. He's acting just
like a little kid now.

00:20:34.059 --> 00:20:37.188
You'll be sorry
if you hurt yourself!

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:42.056
OW! It hurts! SHIRIS!!

00:20:42.133 --> 00:20:45.763
There, there.
It's all right. It doesn't hurt.

00:20:46.404 --> 00:20:48.304
Mommy, milk?

00:20:49.541 --> 00:20:50.804
NOT FROM ME!

00:20:50.875 --> 00:20:52.240
Didn't think it would work...

00:20:55.013 --> 00:20:58.745
Oh, no! Raiden's burning up!
We have to save them!

00:20:59.417 --> 00:21:01.181
No! It'd do no good!

00:21:01.252 --> 00:21:04.187
But, if we don't do something,
then Raiden will...!

00:21:04.255 --> 00:21:06.587
Don't say it, Parn!

00:21:06.891 --> 00:21:08.757
Not in THAT costume...

00:21:09.794 --> 00:21:12.126
How can you act like that...

00:21:12.197 --> 00:21:13.596
...at a time like THIS?!

00:21:13.665 --> 00:21:15.258
Ow!

00:21:17.535 --> 00:21:20.368
And so, Parn and his
friends turn their backs on...

00:21:20.438 --> 00:21:23.874
...the burning city of Raiden and
set off for Fire Dragon Mountain.

00:21:23.942 --> 00:21:26.570
Are you sure this
is the right thing, Parn?!

00:21:26.644 --> 00:21:30.512
| guess, 'cuz it means I can
dress up as SHIRIS next time!

00:21:30.582 --> 00:21:32.277
Oy...

00:22:59.771 --> 00:23:02.672
A desperate battle begins
at Fire Dragon Mountain...

00:23:02.740 --> 00:23:04.333
...with the Scepter
of Domination the prize!

00:23:04.409 --> 00:23:06.309
As sword clashes against sword...

00:23:06.377 --> 00:23:08.846
...as shamanist magic makes
the earth below tremble!

00:23:08.913 --> 00:23:11.211
Its then that Orson sees
with his own eyes...

00:23:11.282 --> 00:23:14.343
...the spirit of anger
which dwells within people.

00:23:14.419 --> 00:23:17.855
Next time, on Record of Lodoss War-
Chronicles of the Heroic Knight:

00:23:17.922 --> 00:23:20.914
Death...
A Gentle Heart Passed On
